WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.989 --> 00:00:05.870
Underworld goddesses, eight-eyed bats, and
an adventurous pet pig who joins our heroine

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.309
on her quest were all chopped from the final
version of Moana!

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:13.250
Yippee ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video, I want to talk about some

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.500
of the fascinating deleted scenes, characters
and rejected concepts that didn't make it

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.369
into the final film of Moana.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:24.539
I've also got a second copy of this amazing
Art of Moana hardback book by Abrams &amp; Chronicle

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:27.119
to give away to a lucky winner on this video.

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:31.669
The book is chock-full of gorgeous concept
art and info on Disney's animated feature,

00:00:31.669 --> 00:00:35.930
and for a chance to win a copy, all you have
to do is subscribe and leave a comment about

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.250
the deleted scenes or story changes on this
video!

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.940
And don't forget that there are bonus ways
to enter the giveaway via the Gleam link in

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.790
the video description below.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.570
As you can imagine, I'll be discussing spoilers
in this video, so if you're not ready for

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:52.010
those, grab the nearest canoe out of here
by clicking the screen for my spoiler-free

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.760
review of Moana.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.270
The beginning of the movie changed quite considerably
over the course of Moana's development with

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:02.120
a number of scenes that featured a lengthier
backstory for Moana being deleted.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.270
So, let's start with toddler Moana who had
one of the movie's most beautiful scenes when

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.420
she first discovered the ocean and the Heart
of Te Fiti.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.790
Originally, to balance that moment out, there
was going to be a much darker scene included

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.060
in the film as well.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:20.280
In that scene, a very young Moana walks out
into the ocean during a storm, and tries to

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.399
control it.

00:01:21.399 --> 00:01:26.719
But the ocean knocks her off a rock and Moana
nearly drowns until her father Chief Tui rescues

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.719
her.

00:01:27.719 --> 00:01:31.189
Although that scene was cut, in the final
movie there is a similar moment of danger

00:01:31.189 --> 00:01:36.079
when an older Moana is shipwrecked after trying
to sail beyond the reef with Pua.

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:40.190
Another cut scene with a young Moana shows
her on a boat together with her father.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:44.670
In the scene, Moana questions why they only
travel between the same three islands when

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.840
there is a whole ocean to explore.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.400
Chief Tui claims that "past the horizon is
the edge of nowhere" and that everything beyond

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:56.299
it was consumed by a land spirit called Te
Po which, by the way, was the movie's original

00:01:56.299 --> 00:01:58.959
name for the lava demon Te Ka.

00:01:58.959 --> 00:02:03.329
During the deleted scene we also get to see
a sweet moment between Moana and the piglet

00:02:03.329 --> 00:02:07.899
Pua who she decides to adopt as her pet pig
as he isn't feeding from his mother with the

00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:09.030
rest of his litter.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:13.860
In fact, in earlier scripts, that very cute
and lovable Kunekune pig was going to join

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:18.350
Moana on her adventure, however, as the story
developed, the filmmakers decided it would

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:22.970
be funnier and better for the story if Moana
ended up stuck with a stupid rooster out on

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.020
the ocean rather than her lovable friend Pua.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:30.530
Speaking of that dumb rooster Heihei, his
character was actually almost scrapped from

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:31.530
the film entirely.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:36.540
He was originally conceived as a type of watchdog
who would keep an eye on Moana for Chief Tui,

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.380
in a role that was similar to how the crab
Sebastian from The Little Mermaid kept watch

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.400
on Ariel for her father Triton.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.230
However, Heihei just wasn't working in the
story drafts and was in serious danger of

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:51.810
being cut completely when (Disney Chief Creative
Officer) John Lasseter gave the scriptwriters

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.180
two days to find a new role for him.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:58.920
In the end, Heihei was dumbed down massively,
and turned into a rooster that liked to swallow

00:02:58.920 --> 00:02:59.920
rocks.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.510
And the scene where the Kakamora attack Moana
and Maui to steal the Heart of Te Fiti was

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:09.320
rewritten to have Heihei complicate the situation
further by swallowing the gem, making the

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.220
crazy rooster the centre of the action.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:15.540
By the way, when John Lasseter decided that
Heihei could remain in the movie, the team

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.480
celebrated with a special meal of fried chicken!

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.070
And there were quite a few other changes and
deleted scenes that affected the set-up of

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.380
Moana's story.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:28.090
One idea was that Moana would have to set
sail in order to rescue her father who had

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.430
got lost at sea.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:34.340
Although this storyline was rejected, an element
of it remained in Chief Tui's backstory, in

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.510
particular the part about how he lost his
friend at sea one day, which became the reason

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.350
why he wouldn't let Moana go beyond the reef.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:45.650
And Chief Tui's fear of voyaging was further
explored in a cut scene where he argued with

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:50.100
Gramma Tala about why Moana shouldn't risk
her life by sailing beyond the reef.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:54.090
In the final movie, this difference of opinion
between Gramma Tala and her son Tui plays

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:58.320
out quite differently, only being touched
upon briefly when he interrupts Gramma Tala

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.770
after her scary tale of Maui and Te Fiti at
the start of the film.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:06.760
In another version of the movie, Moana had
six brothers and there was a scene cut where

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.580
she raced a group of them to prove to her
father that she was the best sailor of them

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:11.580
all.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.630
In the scene, Chief Tui isn't impressed, however,
and refuses to take Moana on the journey he's

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.949
planning to Te Fiti as he says it's too dangerous.

00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:23.430
Although it's a fun scene, with Moana performing
lots of cool manoeuvres to outrace her siblings,

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.189
the movie feels better for leaving out her
brothers and this storyline.

00:04:27.189 --> 00:04:31.550
What's refreshing about the final film is
that the story doesn't just trot out the well-worn

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:35.949
cliché of a girl or woman having to prove
she's just as good as the boys or men around

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:38.650
her to be taken even semi-seriously.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:43.909
In the final version of the movie, Moana automatically
has respect from her father and her community

00:04:43.909 --> 00:04:48.360
who naturally assume that, in time, she will
become the chief of her island.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:53.150
So by scrapping the brother characters, Moana
didn't have to battle sexist attitudes to

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:54.620
succeed in her quest.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:59.430
By the way, there was also an alternate ending
to Moana where she didn't just have six brothers,

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:04.479
but nine brothers, all of whom she needed
to rescue as they were being held hostage.

00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:08.659
Another deleted scene of Moana sailing showed
that she was already a very skilled sailor

00:05:08.659 --> 00:05:10.499
before she embarked on her journey.

00:05:10.499 --> 00:05:15.199
The scene was cut because the filmmakers decided
that if Moana had to learn to sail from Maui,

00:05:15.199 --> 00:05:19.270
it would provide more opportunities for humour
and development between the pair.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:23.830
By the way, this deleted scene also offers
a little peek at Heihei acting more like the

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:28.240
jerk he was in his early incarnation, rather
than the dumb rooster his character was later

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.180
reworked to be.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:35.189
The Realm of Monsters, aka Lalotai or the
underworld, featured numerous scenes, stories

00:05:35.189 --> 00:05:38.400
and characters that, sadly, didn't make it
into the final film.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.669
In one early version, Maui had to enter Lalotai
in disguise as he had enemies that lived in

00:05:43.669 --> 00:05:44.669
the underworld.

00:05:44.669 --> 00:05:48.749
There's actually a little nod to this idea
in the final movie, when Moana dresses up

00:05:48.749 --> 00:05:52.389
as bait to distract Tamatoa while Maui recovers
his fishhook.

00:05:52.389 --> 00:05:57.169
There was also a deleted character called
Hina who guarded the entrance to Lalotai.

00:05:57.169 --> 00:06:01.020
Hina would have been Maui's grandmother in
the movie, and in Polynesian mythology, she

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.189
is a heroic goddess and companion to Maui.

00:06:04.189 --> 00:06:08.180
Mini Maui is a great comedic character in
Moana, but initially he was going to feature

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.430
a lot less in the story.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:13.569
However, it was actually a scene that ended
up being deleted from the movie that was crucial

00:06:13.569 --> 00:06:16.930
to Mini Maui getting more screen time in the
final film.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:21.630
In the deleted scene, Maui jumps down into
the underworld and gets hit by a large rock;

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:26.490
then when he checks on Mini Maui, he discovers
that the little living tattoo is unconscious.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:31.249
Maui tries to wake him up with mouth-to-mouth
resuscitation which leads to Mini Maui springing

00:06:31.249 --> 00:06:33.970
back to life, spluttering and disgusted.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:38.039
When the scene was tested internally at Disney
it had such a good response that it led to

00:06:38.039 --> 00:06:42.219
Mini Maui getting a lot more scenes in the
movie, even though that particular moment

00:06:42.219 --> 00:06:44.620
ended up on the cutting room floor.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:49.409
Also removed from the underworld scenes was
an encounter Moana had with her ancestors,

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:52.340
who helped her with the emotional struggles
she was having on her journey.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:56.900
A different version of this rejected scene
appears in the final film when Moana has a

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:01.861
crisis of confidence after she and Maui initially
fail to restore the heart to Te Ka and Maui

00:07:01.861 --> 00:07:03.059
abandons her.

00:07:03.059 --> 00:07:07.629
The spirit of Gramma Tala and her seafaring
forebears then appear to Moana, singing the

00:07:07.629 --> 00:07:11.909
song of the ancestors, which gives strength
to our heroine who finishes the scene with

00:07:11.909 --> 00:07:14.419
her powerful rendition of 'I am Moana'.

00:07:14.419 --> 00:07:19.479
There's also a scene that was cut for time
where Moana and Maui have to get past an eight-eyed

00:07:19.479 --> 00:07:22.889
bat called Walloo the Wicked on their way
to reach Tamatoa.

00:07:22.889 --> 00:07:27.779
The duo use a pair of conch shells to distract
and confuse the creature while they get past.

00:07:27.779 --> 00:07:32.020
It looks like there might have been an easter
egg to The Little Mermaid's Sebastian in this

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:36.550
scene as Maui pulls out a little red crab
from the shell he's been using!

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:40.699
By the way, the eight-eyed bat creature in
Moana originates from Polynesian legends of

00:07:40.699 --> 00:07:46.089
Maui killing a giant eight-eyed bat that tried
to steal Maui's wife Kumu-lama.

00:07:46.089 --> 00:07:50.389
Concept art and storyboards for Lalotai also
reveal a type of "Yellow Brick Road" that

00:07:50.389 --> 00:07:54.120
Maui and Moana would have followed on their
journey to Tamatoa's Lair.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:58.360
And just before Moana and Maui meet Tamatoa,
there was a deleted song they would have performed

00:07:58.360 --> 00:07:59.999
called "Warrior Face".

00:07:59.999 --> 00:08:04.169
In the song, Maui and Moana psyche themselves
up for their confrontation with the villainous

00:08:04.169 --> 00:08:05.479
giant crab.

00:08:05.479 --> 00:08:09.529
The song was written by Lin-Manuel Miranda
and was based on the Polynesian traditional

00:08:09.529 --> 00:08:10.869
Haka dance.

00:08:10.869 --> 00:08:14.710
It didn't make it into the final film as the
directors felt it showed that Maui and Moana

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.870
were bonding "too early".

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:21.080
The storyboarded scene shows that if the song
had been included it would have been an opportunity

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.680
for a fantastic montage of many other more
strange and wonderful creatures than we already

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.749
saw in the movie's final version of the underworld.

00:08:28.749 --> 00:08:32.349
But that wasn't the only song deleted from
the film; there was another cut song about

00:08:32.349 --> 00:08:33.589
the legend of Maui.

00:08:33.589 --> 00:08:38.169
It was called 'Unstoppable' and combined elements
of Gramma Tala's opening story and Maui's

00:08:38.169 --> 00:08:39.169
song 'You're Welcome.'

00:08:39.169 --> 00:08:44.640
By the way, before the shiny, collecting-obsessed
crab Tamatoa became part of the film, earlier

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:49.370
scripts featured a headless warrior character
who collected things and was based on an Oceanic

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:50.370
myth.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:54.190
However, of course, the headless warrior didn't
speak, so the filmmakers decided to combine

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:58.300
his character with a giant crab character
that, again in earlier scripts, was going

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.709
to attack Moana and Maui at sea.

00:09:00.709 --> 00:09:05.040
And that's how, Tamatoa, as we know him today
in all his blingy-ness, was born.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:09.930
Initially, the Kakamora weren't as aggressive
as they turned out to be in the final film,

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.010
and they weren't little coconut villains either.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:16.720
Instead, they were originally based on Oceanic
legends of the Kakamora who are short, hairy

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:21.490
and mischievous Hobbit-like beings and, according
to head of story David Pimentel, the Kakamora

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.110
in Moana "were going to be little party animals."

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:28.050
However, because the filmmakers wanted them
to pose a real threat to Moana, they made

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:32.301
them much scarier, and inspiration for their
design came from the War Boys in the movie

00:09:32.301 --> 00:09:34.310
Mad Max: Fury Road.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:39.730
Perhaps the craziest concept that was rejected
by the movie's team was a story about a time-travelling

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:40.730
Moana.

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:44.899
Moana, as we know it, is actually set around
2000 years ago, but in the time-travelling

00:09:44.899 --> 00:09:49.600
version of the movie, Moana was a modern girl
who travelled back in time and met her ancestors.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:52.930
So, what do you think about the deleted scenes
and characters?

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:55.720
Are there any you would love to have seen
in the movie?

